{
  "$schema": "https://aka.ms/codetour-schema",
  "title": "Request flow: HTTP to a use case and its ports",
  "description": "Follows POST /api/projects/:id/deployments from the router, through the use case, to the adapters behind its ports.",
  "steps": [
    {
      "file": "janus-go/internal/adapters/httpapi/projects.go",
      "line": 39,
      "title": "The router",
      "description": "`app.Post(\"/api/projects/:id/deployments\"` maps the route to startDeployment. The HTTP layer is a driving adapter."
    },
    {
      "file": "janus-go/internal/adapters/httpapi/deployments.go",
      "line": 20,
      "title": "The driving adapter",
      "description": "`func (a *Server) startDeployment` reads the body, checks the project.deploy policy, and calls the use case. It never touches the Store."
    },
    {
      "file": "janus-go/internal/adapters/fleetnats/fleetnats.go",
      "line": 119,
      "title": "The Fleet port's adapter",
      "description": "`func (c *Client) CreateDeployment`. The single process asks the fleet service over NATS and turns its refusals back into the errors the port documents."
    },
    {
      "file": "janus-go/internal/services/fleet/deployments.go",
      "line": 218,
      "title": "The fleet service checks the build",
      "description": "`func (s *Service) queue`. It asks the builds service for the Build and its Check over NATS, checks the Agent, and only then records the Deployment."
    },
    {
      "file": "janus-go/internal/services/fleet/service.go",
      "line": 54,
      "title": "The Agent link the service needs",
      "description": "`type AgentLink interface`. The fleet service sends commands to Agents through it. Real: agentnats.Link, over the hub's NATS server. Test: agentlinktest.Loopback."
    },
    {
      "file": "janus-go/internal/app/ports.go",
      "line": 15,
      "title": "The Store port",
      "description": "`type Store interface` is what the core reads and writes. It returns typed values and plain errors, and every adapter must pass the contract suite."
    },
    {
      "file": "janus-go/internal/services/fleet/store.go",
      "line": 251,
      "title": "The SQLite store",
      "description": "`func (s *Service) insertDeployment`. Stores the queued Deployment in fleet.db, refusing a second one in flight for the Project in the same transaction."
    },
    {
      "file": "janus-go/internal/domain/deployments/deployments.go",
      "line": 40,
      "title": "A domain rule",
      "description": "`func CanMove` is the legal-moves rule. Adapters call it rather than reimplementing it."
    },
    {
      "file": "janus-go/internal/app/ports.go",
      "line": 178,
      "title": "The Audit port",
      "description": "`type Audit interface` records Audit Events. Recording never fails the caller, so the use case does not handle its errors."
    },
    {
      "file": "janus-go/cmd/janus/services.go",
      "line": 565,
      "title": "The composition root starts the fleet",
      "description": "`func (a *application) startFleet`. It joins the control plane to the tailnet, starts the fleet service, and gives the single process its client."
    }
  ]
}
